From 0e22a280941be0a38e96dee1b4be7335efbc52e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nico-j606 <nico-j606@localhost>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 01:54:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] power: send Qualcomm perf HAL hints for touch and app
 launch

GSIs lack the QTI BoostFramework and some vendor power HALs (e.g. Lenovo
TB-J606 QTI PowerHAL) report Boost.INTERACTION and Mode.LAUNCH as
unsupported, so the CPU is never boosted. Call vendor.qti.hardware.perf
IPerf directly from system_server (a vendor_hal_perf_client) with the
hint ids from the vendor perfboostsconfig.xml:
- touch user activity: 0x1083 (animation boost, both clusters at max
  frequency), 400 ms, re-sent at most every 150 ms
- Mode.LAUNCH: 0x1081 type 1, 2 s, released when the launch ends

No-op when the HAL is absent. Disable with persist.sys.nico.qtiboost=false.

Change-Id: I17b904d6b8983874de9fa6fcc3286c4a5d469a59
